justification:
Pakistani media practitioners faced several safety related
challenges in the period under review. These included a
continuing spate of physical attacks that resulted in the
murder of five journalists, including a citizen journalist;
assault on and injuries sustained by at least six journalists;
arrest or abduction of at least seven journalists; legal
cases or notices faced by at least 15 journalists; attacks
or intimidation of at least five media establishments;
specific threats against journalists in at least four instances;
and several instances of coordinated or violent online
harassment and intimidation of journalists and other
digital information practitioners, including women

IMI researched the content of the most popular Telegram channels and found:
4 out of 16 have a verified channel mark;
5 channels administer the page in Ukrainian;
9 channels are registered in the "News and Media" section, although none of them are professional media;
15 channels left contacts in the "bio" for communication regarding advertising placement;
4 channels are financed by Russian money and spread openly pro-Russian narratives that discredit the Ukrainian authorities.

